# CRAN submission notes for this package

This package was submitted to CRAN before and rejected twice by human reviewers.
Both rejections were for things `R CMD check --as-cran` does not report. Passing
the check is necessary but is not enough. Work through both items below, then run
the check as usual.

## 1. Do not set a seed to a specific number inside a function

CRAN's feedback, verbatim:

> Please do not set a seed to a specific number within a function.

Why it happens: setting a seed inside a function looks like good reproducibility
practice. In fact it silently overwrites the caller's random-number stream, so
the user's own seed is discarded and results change underneath them.

What to do:

- Search every file in `R/` for `set.seed(`.
- No exported function may call `set.seed()` with a fixed value, whether the
  number is written in the call or comes from a hardcoded default.
- If a function needs reproducible randomness, give it a `seed = NULL` argument
  and call `set.seed(seed)` only when the user supplied one. Make sure documented
  defaults, examples, vignettes and tests are updated to match.
- Do not fix this by deleting the call and leaving the tests broken. Randomised
  tests should set their own seed inside the test, not inside the package code.

## 2. Do not use `+ file LICENSE` with a boilerplate LICENSE under GPL

CRAN's feedback, verbatim:

> License components with restrictions and base license permitting such:
> `GPL-3 + file LICENSE`. Please omit `+ file LICENSE` and the file itself, which
> looks like a template for the MIT license. For GPL-3, it is only used to
> specify additional restrictions to the GPL such as attribution requirements.

Why it happens: `usethis::use_mit_license()` writes a two-line template
(`YEAR:` and `COPYRIGHT HOLDER:`). Combined with a GPL-3 `License:` field in
`DESCRIPTION`, that is exactly what CRAN rejected.

What to do:

- Read the `License:` field in `DESCRIPTION` and the `LICENSE` file together.
- If the license is GPL-3 and the `LICENSE` file is only a `YEAR` /
  `COPYRIGHT HOLDER` template, change the field to plain `GPL-3`, delete the
  `LICENSE` file, and remove any reference to it (including in `.Rbuildignore`).

## How these two relate

Both failures came from conventional habits that are wrong for CRAN, not from
carelessness. Do not rely on convention. After fixing the two items above,
re-read the CRAN policy documents for anything else a human reviewer would
object to, then run `R CMD check --as-cran` until it is clean.
